<title>HONG KONG: Hang Seng Bank 1996 net up 6.3 percent.</title>
<headline>Hang Seng Bank 1996 net up 6.3 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   439.0 vs 413.0</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    182.0 vs 230.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil   vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    8,487 vs 7,984</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hang Seng Bank Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  April 2-15</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   April 15</p>
<p>NOTE - Hang Seng Bank is 61.51 percent owned by HSBC Holdings Plc as at April 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 308.0 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of 126 cents) vs 290.0 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
